{"cases":[{"target_alias":"SRC_001","attack":true,"case":"The target's quantitative law is false: stable mixed configurations are not exp(-c n) in expectation. In the configuration model, fix a balanced coloring. The probability that every vertex has at most one opposite-color neighbor is dominated by k=0.3n crossing edges and is exp(-0.458... n), while there are ~2^n balanced colorings, so the expected number of balanced stable mixed configurations is exp((ln 2 - 0.458...)n)=exp(0.235... n). Thus the claimed exponential rarity and the 'non-expanding cut' mechanism fail; a matching of crossing edges can have linear size and expansion bounded away from 0.","counterexample":null,"premise":null,"premise_evidence":null,"successor_question":null}]}